<title>USA: Montana $59.5 mln note deal won by three firms.</title>
<headline>Montana $59.5 mln note deal won by three firms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Montana's $59.5 million tax and revenue anticipation note deal was won by the following three firms Wednesday:</p>
<p>--First Southwest, $34.5 million, 4.50 percent coupon and 3.7481 percent net interest cost.</p>
<p>--Lehman Brothers, $20 million, 4.50 percent coupon and 3.7435 percent NIC.</p>
<p>--Zions Bank, $5 million, 4.50 percent coupon and 3.734 percent NIC.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
